			<abstract>
				<p>int64_t nTimeStart = GetTimeMicros(); // Check it again in case a previous version let a bad block in // NOTE: We don&apos;t currently (re-)invoke ContextualCheckBlock() or // ContextualCheckBlockHeader() here. This means that if we add a new // consensus rule that is enforced in one of those two functions, then we // may have let in a block that violates the rule prior to updating the // software, and we would NOT be enforcing the rule here. Fully solving // upgrade from one software version to the next after a consensus rule // change is potentially tricky and issue-specific (see RewindBlockIndex() // for one general approach that was used for BIP 141 deployment).</p>
